<%#
  Open Settings button + its warning banner (issues #992, #1005)

  The one definition of the way through to the iRaceDeck Settings window, used
  by every place that offers it: `key-bindings-section.ejs` (the 35 action PIs,
  where it closes the bottom section) and `section-header.ejs` (the plugin-level
  `settings.ejs` page, where it sits under the heading).

  The banner above it carries the OPEN failure and only that: the window could
  not be displayed although the settings service is healthy. It has to be HERE
  rather than in the page-top strip that `head-common.ejs` injects, because in
  an action PI that strip is a full scroll away from this button — a user who
  presses it and gets no window would see no explanation at all, which is the
  very failure this warning exists to end.

  The SERVER failure deliberately stays in the top strip instead. It is not
  about this button: with no service a PI has no channel to the plugin, so
  every setting the page can change is inert, and that belongs where the page
  announces page-wide problems.

  `head-common.ejs` gives the top strip the matching `except`, so the open
  banner appears in exactly one place per page. The id literal is duplicated
  from deck-core's SETTINGS_WINDOW_OPEN_WARNING_ID (this bundle is browser code
  and cannot import it); `settings-window-constants.test.ts` guards the pair.

  Parameters:
    - extraClass (String, optional) — appended to the wrapper's class list.
%>
<ird-warnings only="settings-window-open"></ird-warnings>
<div class="ird-open-settings<% if (locals.extraClass) { %> <%= extraClass %><% } %>">
  <ird-open-settings></ird-open-settings>
</div>
